Guard a null class slot in the XFA SOM resolver

`searchNode` dereferences `.isXFAObjectArray` on the result of
`$getChildrenByClass`, which returns `this[name]` verbatim. An absent optional
child is initialized to `null` (`Caption` sets `this.para = null` alongside
`extras`, `font`, `margin` and `value`), so a `.#class` step naming a child the
target does not have throws instead of resolving to nothing.

Reached through `usehref=".#som(...)"` prototype references, which Designer
2024.07 emits and Designer 6.5 does not. DAF Form 1288 carries 43 of them, two
of which point at `#para` on a caption that has only a `<font>`. The throw kills
`Binder.bind()`, so `XFAFactory.form` is never assigned, `_createPagesHelper`
reads `Symbol()` off `undefined`, `dims` is never set, and the document surfaces
as `UnknownErrorException: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading
'length')`.

With the guard, an unresolvable prototype warns and is skipped, which is what
Acrobat does with nothing to inherit. DAF 1288 goes from failing to load to two
pages and 122 fields, every one of them with non-zero width and height and
inside the page box. The other 23 forms in the corpus produce identical page and
field counts before and after.

`children == null` rather than `!children`, so an empty-string slot keeps its
current `[""]` behaviour.

Introduced by PR #13473 (usehref support, merged 2021-06-04) on a line from
commit 45329af9. PR #13761 later hardened every caller of `searchNode` against a
null return "to prevent future bugs" but not the inside of `searchNode`. Still
unguarded on master as of 2026-09-03; no matching issue, PR or Bugzilla report.

--- a/src/core/xfa/som.js
+++ b/src/core/xfa/som.js
@@ -207,9 +207,12 @@
             break;
           case operators.dotHash:
             children = node[$getChildrenByClass](name);
-            children = children.isXFAObjectArray
-              ? children.children
-              : [children];
+            children =
+              children == null
+                ? []
+                : children.isXFAObjectArray
+                  ? children.children
+                  : [children];
             break;
           default:
             break;
@@ -286,7 +289,12 @@
         break;
       case operators.dotHash:
         children = root[$getChildrenByClass](name);
-        children = children.isXFAObjectArray ? children.children : [children];
+        children =
+          children == null
+            ? []
+            : children.isXFAObjectArray
+              ? children.children
+              : [children];
         break;
       default:
         break;
